 "_comment": "Shared geologic map color table for every Ingalls Weather geology map, in any state. Each map unit from any source is crosswalked into ONE of these classes (see geology_sgmc.py for the USGS SGMC crosswalk), so a class has the same color on every map. Order = legend order (water first, then roughly youngest to oldest). 'parent' marks a detail class that a source can only sometimes distinguish (e.g. Imnaha Basalt is mapped separately in Oregon but lumped into the CRB in Washington); its color is a darker shade of the parent's so the two read as one family. A map may also choose not to split a detail class, in which case it is drawn in its parent's color (so the parent color always means 'this family, not split further'). Maps may reword a label for local context (e.g. 'Wallowa batholith granite'), but never recolor a class.",
